   "text": {
    "L1": "Food contains nutrients, and each nutrient has a job in our body.",
    "L2": "Carbohydrates and fats mainly give us energy. Fats give about twice as much energy as the same amount of carbohydrate.",
    "L3": "Rice is mainly a carbohydrate, while ghee is a fat that provides energy.",
    "L4": "Proteins help the body grow and repair itself. Dal, rajma, chana, milk and paneer can provide protein.",
    "L5": "Vitamins and minerals protect us and help the body work well. Fruits and vegetables are useful sources.",
    "L6": "Fibre helps digestion and the passing out of waste. Water helps digest food, carry substances and remove waste.",
    "L7": "Nutritious food need not be costly. Local foods such as dal, chana, amla, guava, leafy vegetables and millets can be rich in nutrients.",
    "L8": "So a healthy plate brings together different foods for energy, growth, protection, digestion and body processes."
   },
